    "turn_text": "Hi, I'm Susan Swain, host of C-Spans Q&A, where we spend an hour with non-fiction writers and historians who add context to today's news. Adam Smith, a longtime Democratic congressman from Washington State, has served in public office since his first campaign for state senate at age 25. For much of that time, he has struggled with bouts of anxiety and depression, later coupled with debilitating chronic pain. He captures it all in his new book, Lost and Broken, and joins us this week to discuss his efforts to find the right treatments, estimating that he's seen more than 100 healthcare professionals all while navigating his busy congressional schedule. We also discuss his observations about the U.S. healthcare system and his thoughts about the need for more social acceptance of Americans with physical and mental health issues. Our conversation will begin in just a moment. Hey, it's Ryan Reynolds here",
