    "turn_text": "well, I like the subtitle, my journey back from chronic pain, crippling anxiety. The basic title isn't the most optimistic in the world, but there is a path back. So, yes. What is the story you tell in the book? Well, basically, I went through a bout of anxiety and chronic pain. And the only struggle to explain it is there were lifelong aspects of it. I mean, this is stuff that I was feeling, you know, gosh, when I was a kid, high stress, I had anxiety then. and I actually had a knee injury when I was 12 years old that manifested itself out. But I dealt with it without any significant problems until I was 40 when I had an uncontrollable bout of anxiety that lasted about five months. And then, about eight years after that, the anxiety came back and I couldn't find a way out of it. And then shortly thereafter, chronic pain set in, I had three hip surgeries. And that whole thing lasted about six years of struggling to figure out what's wrong with me and what do I do about it. It was a very difficult six-year period.",
