  {
    "episode_id": 86213,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86213.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, originally I decided to want to write about it because I wanted to sort of capture what happened. So I was coming out of it, you know, mid-2019 was when I finally started to feel better, close to where I was at. Well, I guess, you know, the last, I finally got off all the medications I was taking in April of 2019. That was the last time. And then the physical therapy and the psychotherapy had been kicking in. And I was like, so what happens? Fresh in my mind, I want to write it down, then the pandemic hit. So I had a lot of time. So I wrote it just to sort of keep it fresh in my mind and to remember what happened. And then as I was writing it, and as I was thinking about other people, I mean, tens of millions of people suffer from some combination of anxiety, depression, or chronic pain. And I thought it would be a story that would be helpful in the larger debate about how do we address those challenges that so many people face.",
