    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, the number one biggest thing is universal access to health care. Now, that does not solve the whole problem. But there are too many people out there who don't have insurance. So, you know, you will struggle to find a solution. Now, I will say that of those hundred plus Probably over half of them didn't take insurance. Okay, so that's part of the problem as well. But certainly universal access to healthcare. Second big thing is let's emphasize primary care that the doctors who are supposed to look at you holistically. And the third thing is we are way too reliant on drugs and surgeries. That is sort of the easy button in healthcare. It's expensive and it oftentimes makes the problem worse.",
