    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "that? No, it was cathartic. I didn't find it difficult at all. I think the biggest thing about it for me is I'm an excessively logical person. I love to be able to explain things. Like even now, I'm going to have a budget town hall in a couple of weeks to talk about the deficit. And I'm fascinated to sort of walk through. Here's the deficit. Here's the debt. Here's the debt ceiling. Here's what's really going on. So for me, this was like explaining it. So what happened? Okay, how did I wind up in this place in the first place? And then how did I work my way out of it and what were the lessons that were learned? So it was like, well, I'm not really solving the puzzle because at that point the puzzle had been solved. It was understanding how I solved the puzzle. And I found that fascinating.",
