    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86213.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, the origin story actually starts with I was adopted. So I was actually born at George Washington University Hospital. My biological mother was in the foreign service at the time. She was a code clerk. I was conceived in Prague, but they were not married, and my biological father didn't want to have anything to do with it. So my biological mother gave me up for adoption to her older brother, who was living in C-TAC and working for United Airlines at the time. So I was born to Rochester University Hospital. 10 days later, flown to CTAC, and that's where I grew up. But I did not know that I was adopted. Nobody ever told me until after both my parents had passed away. And my biological mother, who I had grown up thinking was my aunt, sent me a letter explaining it to me.",
