    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Quite a bit, actually. I'm a very philosophical person. Beyond what I wasn't raised, religious. That was one of the agreements with the adoption was I was supposed to be raised to Piscopalian. I was baptized, never quite worked out. But I was always very interested in those subjects in philosophy, meaning of life, theology. And let me tell you, the Jesuits are a great group of people to hang out with if you want to think about that stuff and study it. So it was a really good education.",
