    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86213.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Mine was at a slightly higher level. I was afraid of a lot of things, particularly new experiences interacting with people. I was afraid of heights. I was afraid of being on the water. I was really afraid of interacting with people that I didn't know. At the same time, I was a pretty ambitious competitive person. Sports were a great outlet for that until I screwed up my knee and my arm and a bunch of other things. By the time I was 13 or 14, I really couldn't play that effectively. But sports just gave me a place to go and just have some focus. But yeah, I was very insecure and very ambitious at the same time. I mentioned the trip to Fordham and the education. The biggest thing about Fordham was just, I'm going to New York.",
