    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86213.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 49,
    "turn_text": "Because my father, I mean, that's the initial draw was he was the secretary treasurer of his union. He was never that involved, but he was interested in politics and subjects. And that's what he sort of wanted to push me into. And then as I got into it, You know, I had this sense that despite all of that insecurity, that I had leadership qualities, that I liked to solve problems and bring people together to try to find out how to resolve differences. I liked doing that. I liked sort of bringing peace and order to the immediate world around me. So I thought it was something that I could do. And also, as I document in the book, I thought it was my destiny. I just, I just did. Okay, whatever forces in the universe there are, I thought this was what I was supposed to do. And then I was like, this is what I'm supposed to do, but you know, so I just, I forced myself forward. In fact, I document in the book, you know, I was terrified of the water. So I wasn't going to swim, but they were taking us to swimming lessons in the fourth grade. And I refused to even try until like halfway through the class one day, I just jumped in the water. I said, well, at some point I'm going to have to do this. So let's just give it a shot.",
