    "turn_text": "was the big thing, you know, because I did not have confidence prior I had the sense of ambition, but I also thought You know, I'm not going to be able to get there. I have a lack of confidence. But when I won that election, I had confidence. And then I found out I was actually pretty good at it. You know, if I wasn't there all the time, if I could just think and interact with people that I, you know, sort of knew how to do this. And, you know, I was fortunate as well. I got to chair the Judiciary Committee two years after I was elected the State Senate. Seton Congress was available. It was a tough campaign against an incumbent Republican, but I got there. And turned out, you know, with a little bit of confidence, I was pretty good at it. Now, during that timeframe, as I document, it was a high stress thing. I mean, my general approach to getting through these difficult challenges was as I documented, think, think, think, work, work, worry, worry, worry. That's what I did. Oh, and it's over. I finally relax. Okay. after a certain amount of point, if you're that intense and not stressed. And meanwhile, my knee and my back and a bunch of other things were not working great at the time either. But I got through it.",
