    "turn_text": "you know, the whole thing and the drugs throughout this whole process and this half dozen different drugs or maybe more that I took throughout the whole thing. Some of them helped. Some of them didn't. But even the ones that helped, I was constantly worried about the fact that one of the side effects and I'm going to build up tolerance. And I absolutely built up tolerance to Clonazepam. That was the benzodaphamine that I used. And it didn't work as well after that. But the first time, never having taken it before. It was a miracle. But even while I'm doing it, I'm like, yeah, I can't rely on this. So I take one or a couple days. I went and saw the psychiatrist, I documented that in the book. It's hard to explain. I don't know what exactly he was trying to accomplish. But I didn't understand what he was talking about or what was going on. But four or five months after that, I just stopped taking the class of Pam and eventually I calmed down and got better.",
